Error [E0211]: `Res?` can't be copied out of the place it is read from
  --> tests/ui/resource_forwarded_out_of_place.jet:18:12
    |
 18 |     r :: h.first ?? return 0
    |            ^^^^^
 Why: It holds a resource, which has one cleanup owner; this position takes an owned value, so the copy and the place would both close the same resource
 Fix: Use it where it is, or take `h` with the move marker `^` (a `^` parameter or receiver) and move the field out with `^`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0211

Error [E0201]: `env` cannot be moved from borrowed storage
  --> tests/ui/resource_forwarded_out_of_place.jet:23:10
    |
 23 |     r :: env ?? return 0
    |          ^^^
 Why: `env` is a read or write parameter, so its caller keeps the value, and `Res?` can't be copied into an owned value
 Fix: Declare the parameter `^` so the caller hands the value over
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0201

